I accidentally duplicated `state.ownedTools[type] = true;`. Remove. Also `popGroundItem(item)` called at start, then in branch for wall/campfire we don't return and then call `popGroundItem(item)` again at bottom—double pop with same item but it's already popping, so harmless; but cleaner to restructure. Let's rewrite collectUpgradeItem cleanly:

```
function collectUpgradeItem(item) {
 if (!item || item.popping >0) return false;
 const type=item.type;
 popGroundItem(item);
 if (type === 'ironWall') { createIronWall(...); showToast(...); }
 else if (type==='biggerCampfire') { applyBiggerCampfire(); }
 else if isTool: { state.ownedTools[type]=true; update...; showToast; playUpgradeChime(); equipTool(type); return true; }
 updateHud(); playPickupSound(); return true;
}
```
