content.text:
Oops, `updateIronRocks` regrow animation logic wrong: when broken group hidden; when regrow, broken=false, group.scale set 0.6 then targetScale = rock.scale * (rock.broken ? 0.8 : 1) = rock.scale, so it grows to full. good. Shake rotation. Fine. But there is no per-frame update of rock group position; static.

But when `rock.hits` decremented but not broken, visual crack? We could shrink slightly. We set targetScale full. To show cracks, maybe not. Requirement "cracks it" - shake and toast. Could add crack visible by scaling main chunk? Maybe we can add a crack material overlay. Simpler: when hit, scale to `rock.scale*(1 - (hitsMax-hits)*0.08)`? But hit not reflected. Let's adjust `updateIronRocks` targetScale based on hits:
```
const damageRatio = rock.hits / rock.hitsMax;
const targetScale = rock.scale * (0.8 + damageRatio*0.2) maybe after one hit -> 0.9, then break.
```
But regrow sets hits max. Let's modify later maybe. Not crucial.

Now machine functions and panel.

Design functions:
- `renderUpgradeOptions()` once or each open to update affordability. We'll build DOM once on first call, and update classes each `updateMachinePanel`.
- `buildUpgradeOptions()`:
```
UPGRADE_ORDER.forEach(key => {
 const up = UPGRADES[key];
 const btn = document.createElement('button'); btn.type='button'; btn.className='upgrade-card'; btn.dataset.upgrade=key;
 btn.innerHTML = `<span class="upgrade-name">${up.name}</span><span class="upgrade-cost">...</span><span class="upgrade-desc">${up.desc}</span>`;
 btn.addEventListener('pointerdown', e => {e.preventDefault(); e.stopPropagation(); startUpgrade(key)});
 upgradeGrid.appendChild(btn);
})
```
Need use textContent to avoid injection, but constants safe. Fine.
- `updateMachinePanel()`:
